# Keeping the build context small matters: the repository root is the
# context, and shipping the .git directory, the docs and the test fixtures to
# the daemon on every build is the difference between a two second and a
# thirty second upload. Everything the server build needs is go.mod, go.sum
# and the Go sources (plus what they go:embed, which lives beside them).
.git
.github
.playwright-mcp
docs
*.md
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
*.png
dist
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
examples/deploy-gcp/analytics
examples/deploy-gcp/ci-setup.sh
examples/deploy-gcp/cloudbuild.yaml
examples/deploy-gcp/cloudrun.yaml
examples/deploy-gcp/monitoring
examples/deploy-gcp/release.yml.example
examples/docker-compose

# The one Markdown file the image ships: the licence notices for the modules
# linked into the server binary. It is copied into the final stage, so it
# must reach the context despite the *.md rule above.
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
